[{:db/id "q-22056/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "d66cd3fb-68ef-5e9f-8738-c4ecb686ba8d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-22056/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "8e31435a-3348-5fd6-a47f-3b01176c93d4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-22056/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "83ac9905-b3d3-5121-a0af-d8d82ac98cf6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-22056/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "754569d8-841e-5f10-85f5-f157644a1661" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-22056/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "c3d93bad-fcc3-5732-9a35-6b1f87e389be" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-22056/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2c53eec0-77cb-51af-871b-575a15bbc493" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-22056/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer-field/choices ["q-22056/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-22056/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-22056/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-22056/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-22056/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-22056" :question/id #uuid "960a6f14-6ea1-5d58-9c80-cf93ecc61484" :question/math-academy-id "q-22056" :question/problem "$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,S=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1 & 8\\end{aligned}],\\,T=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $R,S,$ and $T?$\n\n- The product $SR$ is well defined\n- The product $RS$ is well defined\n- The product $ST$ is well defined" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $R$ is a $4\\times 2$ matrix, $S$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix, and $T$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nThere are $4$ columns in $S$ and $4$ rows in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $S$ equals the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $S$ and $R$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{S}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{4}}}{\\times }_{✓}{R}_{\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $2$ columns in $R$ and $2$ rows in $S.$ Since the number of columns in $R$ equals the number of rows in $S,$ the matrices $R$ and $S$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{R}_{4\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{✓}{S}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 4}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $4$ columns in $S$ and $3$ rows in $T.$ Since the number of columns in $S$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $T,$ the matrices $S$ and $T$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{S}_{2\\times 4}{\\times }_{\\ne }{T}_{3\\times 2}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statements I and II are true, while statement III is false." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-22056/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b494140f-206a-5317-8079-ff719a253140"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-22056"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-42374"] :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 1 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ -0 & 6\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statement are true regarding the matrices $A,B,$ and $C?$\n\n- The product $AB$ is well defined\n- The product $BA$ is well defined\n- The product $AC$ is well defined" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $A$ is a $4\\times 2$ matrix, $B$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix, and $C$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nThere are $2$ columns in $A$ and $2$ rows in $B.$ Since the number of columns in $A$ equals the number of rows in $B,$ the matrices $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{4\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 4}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $4$ columns in $B$ and $4$ rows in $A.$ Since the number of columns in $B$ equals the number of rows in $A,$ the matrices $B$ and $A$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{B}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{4}}}{\\times }_{✓}{A}_{\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $2$ columns in $A$ and $2$ rows in $C.$ Since the number of columns in $A$ equals the number of rows in $C,$ the matrices $A$ and $C$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{4\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{✓}{C}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that all three statements are true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-42375/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "d2e04d10-c7e2-5141-8bc2-c81477b672ab" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42375/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "ecefff85-a6bb-5327-83d4-977fd4f803fd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42375/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "dc79beda-e403-5b60-b642-9464d319dd19" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42375/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "1729579d-d89c-5b6b-8624-392ec00d7675" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42375/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "c02960f7-95ee-5842-91e7-fbb72d11cb9f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42375/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1d19f388-3e5d-5ebc-bf16-0563f40d77db" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-42375/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer-field/choices ["q-42375/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-42375/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-42375/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-42375/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-42375/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-42375" :question/id #uuid "fbab72a2-b996-5451-a2ce-a24571b5c158" :question/math-academy-id "q-42375" :question/problem "$$\nJ=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 7\\end{aligned}],\\,K=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ 8 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,L=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -9 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $J,K,$ and $L?$\n\n- The product $JK$ is well defined\n- The product $KL$ is well defined\n- The product $JL$ is well defined" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $J$ is a $3\\times 4$ matrix, $K$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, and $L$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix.\n\nThere are $4$ columns in $J$ and $3$ rows in $K.$ Since the number of columns in $J$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $K,$ the matrices $J$ and $K$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{J}_{3\\times 4}{\\times }_{\\ne }{K}_{3\\times 2}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $2$ columns in $K$ and $2$ rows in $L.$ Since the number of columns in $K$ equals the number of rows in $L$, the matrices $K$ and $L$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{K}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{✓}{L}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 4}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $4$ columns in $J$ and $2$ rows in $L.$ Since the number of columns in $J$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $L$, the matrices $J$ and $L$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{J}_{3\\times 4}{\\times }_{\\ne }{L}_{2\\times 4}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statement II is true, while statements I and III are false." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-42375/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b494140f-206a-5317-8079-ff719a253140"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-42375"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-42376/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "3009f0f1-8099-5948-b069-b058dbb85aeb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42376/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "1fbbea6d-f080-52cc-b876-0e0125d2126f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42376/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "479c1103-d4e0-5535-9ee1-05bf4b89f050" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42376/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "632fab21-2f5c-5acb-83d2-2291286ba0bb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42376/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "c75e3436-363d-5234-9b3e-ee511126cc77" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42376/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5cf9b8d0-4482-546b-bbc0-5fed1ba7f873" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-42376/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-42376/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-42376/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-42376/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-42376/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-42376/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-42376" :question/id #uuid "5a11eab4-94a2-5361-9f1e-16fe3bcd7ce1" :question/math-academy-id "q-42376" :question/problem "$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,E=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,F=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $D,E,$ and $F?$\n\n- The product $ED$ is well defined\n- The product $FD$ is well defined\n- The product $EF$ is well defined" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $D$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix, $E$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, and $F$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix.\n\nThere are $2$ columns in $E$ and $2$ rows in $D.$ Since the number of columns in $E$ equals the number of rows in $D,$ the matrices $E$ and $D$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{E}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{✓}{D}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $3$ columns in $F$ and $2$ rows in $D.$ Since the number of columns in $F$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $D,$ the matrices $F$ and $D$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{F}_{2\\times 3}{\\times }_{\\ne }{D}_{2\\times 2}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $2$ columns in $E$ and $2$ rows in $F.$ Since the number of columns in $E$ equals the number of rows in $F,$ the matrices $E$ and $F$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{E}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{✓}{F}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 3}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statements I and III are true, while statement II is false." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-42376/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b494140f-206a-5317-8079-ff719a253140"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-42376"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-22063"] :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 7 \\\\ 8 & 8 & 8\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $A,B,$ and $C?$\n\n- The product $AB$ is well defined\n- The product $BA$ is well defined\n- The product $AC$ is well defined" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix, $B$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, and $C$ is a $3\\times 1$ column vector\n\nThere are $3$ columns in $A$ and $3$ rows in $B.$ Since the number of columns in $A$ equals the number of rows in $B,$ the matrices $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\times }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $2$ columns in $B$ and $3$ rows in $A.$ Since the number of columns in $B$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $A,$ the matrices $B$ and $A$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{B}_{3\\times 2}{\\times }_{\\ne }{A}_{3\\times 3}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $3$ columns in $A$ and $3$ rows in $C.$ Since the number of columns in $A$ equals the number of rows in $C,$ the matrices $A$ and $C$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\times }_{✓}{C}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 1}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statements I and III are true, while statement II is false." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-70702/selection/277a529ddac913b6a125a1f0be546869cbf1175ab173fe66a1341f64e0e9ef5a" :answer/id #uuid "ac99cb50-da9b-5e97-85b6-1d4d301c9904" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\times 3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70702/selection/e2e854358beca7b69d17bdedb75ac35a580d242bffd2d3ef8661465384e0f544" :answer/id #uuid "371f37c5-c633-5a3c-83cf-40238403a1db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\times 5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70702/selection/5b5d1bc8de70e83925e9819642e59f14b309a85b16af811af5caf3fd3de22f6d" :answer/id #uuid "a71cc80d-e6a2-53e4-804e-56daf70ada7c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\times 5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70702/selection/67e2f68495bf59024298cc5a843e3c22980b8438c9ec5b0733bc7ed8ce150777" :answer/id #uuid "6654e2f1-6a95-55cb-9273-d21aed8511e0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The product is undefined" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70702/selection/8e5835c0f403c8fe873d835d95621e2788ed3af7edddb5cc2ae4be47293fc